From f68353adc5b3277b46790f9eedf068f38d1af790 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:02:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/21] Meta+Everywhere: Add LADYBIRD_LEGACY_MACOS for macOS
 without Metal or IOSurface

Metal never existed on PowerPC and the IOSurface framework only appeared
in 10.6, yet every `#ifdef AK_OS_MACOS` in the GPU path assumed both.
With LADYBIRD_LEGACY_MACOS=ON the build:

- defines AK_MACOS_HAS_IOSURFACE / AK_MACOS_HAS_METAL only when not in
  legacy mode, and gates the Metal Skia backend, the IOSurface backing
  stores, the WebGL (Metal-ANGLE) context and the related helper-process
  plumbing on those macros, falling back to CPU painting and no WebGL
  exactly like a Linux build without Vulkan;
- leaves MetalContext.mm and IOSurface.cpp out of the build and drops
  the Metal and IOSurface framework links (CoreFoundation, CoreServices,
  Foundation and Accelerate stay), compiling TimeZoneWatcherMacOS.mm
  (pure CoreFoundation C API) as C++ for GCC;
- uses fontconfig for fonts instead of CoreText, with the macOS system
  font directories added to the search path;
- falls back to pthread_mach_thread_np() and the Component Manager
  audio APIs when the deployment target is older than 10.6 (the audio
  fallback is untested), and shims MSG_NOSIGNAL for SDKs older than
  10.13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
